[{:db/id 17592186059757 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-06d7e42a-14b7-5ba4-9656-a3c1d06d273b" "question-da13acd8-77ae-5f2b-ba9c-504353353d52"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186059566 :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}6x+4y=1 \\\\ x-8y-z=-2 \\\\ 3x+2y-2z=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n![](images/21/212a3beac5ede3786bad835a693b0a725f331de41d6969dce7f17925dde012d7.svg)\n\nWhat are the values of $a,$ $b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}6x+4y+0z=1 \\\\ x-8y-z=-2 \\\\ 3x+2y-2z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n![](images/22/22034036ec7859b56e9e19124e33fa616eddfc3784e15f8074583e28253a4bae.svg)\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n![](images/b5/b5e0f47e7c4bb15e8923bceb665dcc87944090e3a39f9a335b17ab0b85025cc8.svg)\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n![](images/b6/b643463daef16c2179d6f6320d31353a23b042f3774295eb55e48af0242ec655.svg)\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n![](images/bf/bf8fb79fd8998c5c867fc371535e26f2e92bea5fa7262789bd44aea07e24f93c.svg)\n\nTherefore, $a=6,$ $b=2,$ and $c=-2.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186059758 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5bfaecd0-980e-55a7-befc-289a7a9c5c34" "question-87b42522-bb27-5dd3-ac3e-bd3279e82fdf"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186059567 :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z=4 \\\\ z-x+2=-1 \\\\ 2y-2x-4z=-4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n![](images/22/228e4520f4301ac7acb7eef54fad6dcc8ce9bbf43d48124a761978dfcea6423b.svg)\nWhat are the values of $a,$ $b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z=4 \\\\ -x+0y+z=-3 \\\\ -2x+2y-4z=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n![](images/80/80100c3398fa2eac3a07696dd30354c3c971f0650ab32d67a958492ed1cbdeae.svg)\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n![](images/8f/8f7fdfc0426ad23a34e6d7f2915181a88a63ea74da93b2b6bd718e03f21ba8d2.svg)\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n![](images/28/2867d40f70d0e042e522e1bb14ea8af830e42f22a63cc482ba67923c51807312.svg)\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n![](images/9a/9a4c39673ffd559b35ed9dbf0e465f6a8714c0d9a467178a51e1f6ad79a81445.svg)\n\nTherefore $a=0,$ $b=-2,$ $c=-3.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-06d7e42a-14b7-5ba4-9656-a3c1d06d273b" :question/id #uuid "06d7e42a-14b7-5ba4-9656-a3c1d06d273b" :question/math-academy-id "q-10006" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}x-z=0 \\\\ x+y+3z=2 \\\\ 3x-2y+z=4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & b \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ a & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ c \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x+0y-z=0 \\\\ x+y+3z=2 \\\\ 3x-2y+z=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=3,\\,b=-1,\\,c=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-456a058b-2a76-50e4-b196-28caf276666d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-456a058b-2a76-50e4-b196-28caf276666d" :answer-field/id #uuid "456a058b-2a76-50e4-b196-28caf276666d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-01601b6f-c05d-574c-9a4a-d776d7830de4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a3f35897-b61a-57d6-81d6-9ea4cf4754e2" "answer-df865a24-76e9-5e0c-aef0-ccb73198892d" "answer-f375eeb9-cae0-5b47-8162-0ab390a8e5ce" "answer-4d9e88a0-7c5e-5e8c-9e9a-14296af074a8" "answer-01601b6f-c05d-574c-9a4a-d776d7830de4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a3f35897-b61a-57d6-81d6-9ea4cf4754e2" :answer/id #uuid "a3f35897-b61a-57d6-81d6-9ea4cf4754e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=-2,\\,b=1,\\,c=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-df865a24-76e9-5e0c-aef0-ccb73198892d" :answer/id #uuid "df865a24-76e9-5e0c-aef0-ccb73198892d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=-3,\\,b=1,\\,c=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f375eeb9-cae0-5b47-8162-0ab390a8e5ce" :answer/id #uuid "f375eeb9-cae0-5b47-8162-0ab390a8e5ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=1,\\,b=3,\\,c=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4d9e88a0-7c5e-5e8c-9e9a-14296af074a8" :answer/id #uuid "4d9e88a0-7c5e-5e8c-9e9a-14296af074a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=2,\\,b=-1,\\,c=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-01601b6f-c05d-574c-9a4a-d776d7830de4" :answer/id #uuid "01601b6f-c05d-574c-9a4a-d776d7830de4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=3,\\,b=-1,\\,c=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-da13acd8-77ae-5f2b-ba9c-504353353d52" :question/id #uuid "da13acd8-77ae-5f2b-ba9c-504353353d52" :question/math-academy-id "q-36179" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x+5z=5 \\\\ -x+5y-3z=2 \\\\ x-4y+7z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & a & 5 \\\\ b & 5 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 7\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x+0y+5z=5 \\\\ -x+5y-3z=2 \\\\ x-4y+7z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 7\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=0,\\,b=-1,\\,c=5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-83a4688c-a103-5974-9014-77e44fbfd4ee"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-83a4688c-a103-5974-9014-77e44fbfd4ee" :answer-field/id #uuid "83a4688c-a103-5974-9014-77e44fbfd4ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ccaa4421-7462-521e-bd86-4c7357d0d8ca" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ccaa4421-7462-521e-bd86-4c7357d0d8ca" "answer-fc3f9e0f-2358-5b78-8d1f-f66161800384" "answer-62f10e81-bf0b-5d8f-abd5-66b9009b22b7" "answer-223847b6-00fc-5235-8827-7e678d11053d" "answer-ca5cbda7-94a5-56d2-8e39-bf95cd46be03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ccaa4421-7462-521e-bd86-4c7357d0d8ca" :answer/id #uuid "ccaa4421-7462-521e-bd86-4c7357d0d8ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=0,\\,b=-1,\\,c=5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fc3f9e0f-2358-5b78-8d1f-f66161800384" :answer/id #uuid "fc3f9e0f-2358-5b78-8d1f-f66161800384" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=0,\\,b=-4,\\,c=5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-62f10e81-bf0b-5d8f-abd5-66b9009b22b7" :answer/id #uuid "62f10e81-bf0b-5d8f-abd5-66b9009b22b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=1,\\,b=-3,\\,c=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-223847b6-00fc-5235-8827-7e678d11053d" :answer/id #uuid "223847b6-00fc-5235-8827-7e678d11053d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=1,\\,b=-3,\\,c=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ca5cbda7-94a5-56d2-8e39-bf95cd46be03" :answer/id #uuid "ca5cbda7-94a5-56d2-8e39-bf95cd46be03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a=5,\\,b=0,\\,c=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186299537 :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-y+z=0 \\\\ 5x+y-7z=-2 \\\\ -2x+4y+3z=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | $3$ | $-1$ | $1$ |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | {{field-1}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | {{field-2}} | $1$ | {{field-3}} |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | $-2$ |  | . |\n|  |  | $-2$ | {{field-4}} | $3$ |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | $4$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-y+z=0 \\\\ 5x+y-7z=-2 \\\\ -2x+4y+3z=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 1 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 1 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186265930 :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x+y+7z=5 \\\\ x-4y+8z=1 \\\\ -6y+9z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -4 & b \\\\ 0 & a & 9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b,$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x+y+7z=5 \\\\ x-4y+8z=1 \\\\ 0x-6y+9z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 9\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-6,\\,b=8,\\,c=5.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186060276 :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-4y+z=2 \\\\ x-6y+11z=3 \\\\ 3x-4y-z=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 & a \\\\ 1 & b & c \\\\ 3 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186345096 :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}-y+z=1 \\\\ 2z+y+x=-1 \\\\ 3y-z+x=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & b \\\\ 1 & c & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}0x-y+z=1 \\\\ x+y+2z=-1 \\\\ x+3y-z=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=0,\\,b=2,\\,c=3.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-5bfaecd0-980e-55a7-befc-289a7a9c5c34" :question/id #uuid "5bfaecd0-980e-55a7-befc-289a7a9c5c34" :question/math-academy-id "q-317636" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2z+3x-5=4 \\\\ 6z-4y+3=15 \\\\ 7y+2x-2=11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | $3$ | $0$ | {{field-1}} |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | {{field-2}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} | $-4$ | $6$ |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | $12$ |  | . |\n|  |  | $2$ | {{field-4}} | $0$ |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | $13$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+0y+2z=9 \\\\ 0x-4y+6z=12 \\\\ 2x+7y+0z=13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 13\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 13\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a0491ce2-8d7c-51ed-99a4-858a23cff123" "answer-field-858e4e65-7369-5bb6-9760-59c91beb24f5" "answer-field-28353e39-acc8-5471-9aa6-69d0698d44c5" "answer-field-d7de047a-a7eb-5fa7-82bc-f250f9e7cda3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a0491ce2-8d7c-51ed-99a4-858a23cff123" :answer-field/id #uuid "a0491ce2-8d7c-51ed-99a4-858a23cff123" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-0e1d1b7d-645c-539e-8352-b3dfb9ffcd03" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0e1d1b7d-645c-539e-8352-b3dfb9ffcd03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0e1d1b7d-645c-539e-8352-b3dfb9ffcd03" :answer/id #uuid "0e1d1b7d-645c-539e-8352-b3dfb9ffcd03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-858e4e65-7369-5bb6-9760-59c91beb24f5" :answer-field/id #uuid "858e4e65-7369-5bb6-9760-59c91beb24f5" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-e1bb35e7-e173-5077-9b70-1eca4b1960a8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e1bb35e7-e173-5077-9b70-1eca4b1960a8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e1bb35e7-e173-5077-9b70-1eca4b1960a8" :answer/id #uuid "e1bb35e7-e173-5077-9b70-1eca4b1960a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-28353e39-acc8-5471-9aa6-69d0698d44c5" :answer-field/id #uuid "28353e39-acc8-5471-9aa6-69d0698d44c5" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-f600605e-c432-5a49-8937-87085525ad30" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f600605e-c432-5a49-8937-87085525ad30"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f600605e-c432-5a49-8937-87085525ad30" :answer/id #uuid "f600605e-c432-5a49-8937-87085525ad30" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d7de047a-a7eb-5fa7-82bc-f250f9e7cda3" :answer-field/id #uuid "d7de047a-a7eb-5fa7-82bc-f250f9e7cda3" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-1b7db70e-4c06-5847-ae4c-8d2d12c80e8b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1b7db70e-4c06-5847-ae4c-8d2d12c80e8b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1b7db70e-4c06-5847-ae4c-8d2d12c80e8b" :answer/id #uuid "1b7db70e-4c06-5847-ae4c-8d2d12c80e8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186299547 :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2z-2y-5x=5 \\\\ -3z+3y+4x=1 \\\\ 2z-2x+y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | $-5$ | {{field-1}} | $2$ |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | $5$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $4$ | $3$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | {{field-3}} |  | . |\n|  |  | $-2$ | {{field-4}} | $2$ |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | $2$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-5x-2y+2z=5 \\\\ 4x+3y-3z=1 \\\\ -2x+y+2z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186299629 :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5x-3y+4=7 \\\\ -2x+6z-1=8 \\\\ 7y-5z+2=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | $5$ | {{field-1}} | $0$ |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | {{field-2}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $-2$ | {{field-3}} | $6$ |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | $9$ |  | . |\n|  |  | {{field-4}} | $7$ | $-5$ |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | $-5$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5x-3y+0z=3 \\\\ -2x+0y+6z=9 \\\\ 0x+7y-5z=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-87b42522-bb27-5dd3-ac3e-bd3279e82fdf" :question/id #uuid "87b42522-bb27-5dd3-ac3e-bd3279e82fdf" :question/math-academy-id "q-317519" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}8y+6x-3z+4=0 \\\\ 5z-3y+x-6=0 \\\\ 7x-4z-y-9=0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | $8$ | $-3$ |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | $-4$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $1$ | $-3$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | {{field-3}} |  | . |\n|  |  | {{field-4}} | $-1$ | $-4$ |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | $9$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}6x+8y-3z=-4 \\\\ x-3y+5z=6 \\\\ 7x-y-4z=9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 8 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -1 & -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}6 & 8 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -1 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-58b5d536-1639-5442-8db5-05c5714eee02" "answer-field-3858435e-6d82-5994-86f0-620119922670" "answer-field-75499a87-c853-5d3b-8493-31cc1387404a" "answer-field-3dca1250-a568-5b14-aa99-ede3c01994fe"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-58b5d536-1639-5442-8db5-05c5714eee02" :answer-field/id #uuid "58b5d536-1639-5442-8db5-05c5714eee02" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-d3575d9f-b5c1-5e4f-8e61-3fb7541222f0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d3575d9f-b5c1-5e4f-8e61-3fb7541222f0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d3575d9f-b5c1-5e4f-8e61-3fb7541222f0" :answer/id #uuid "d3575d9f-b5c1-5e4f-8e61-3fb7541222f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3858435e-6d82-5994-86f0-620119922670" :answer-field/id #uuid "3858435e-6d82-5994-86f0-620119922670" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-8600538f-009c-502c-8f93-c0f999bc2b02" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8600538f-009c-502c-8f93-c0f999bc2b02"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8600538f-009c-502c-8f93-c0f999bc2b02" :answer/id #uuid "8600538f-009c-502c-8f93-c0f999bc2b02" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-75499a87-c853-5d3b-8493-31cc1387404a" :answer-field/id #uuid "75499a87-c853-5d3b-8493-31cc1387404a" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-eefcde1b-d3b8-55ec-9bff-1b6b1e19f657" :answer-field/choices ["answer-eefcde1b-d3b8-55ec-9bff-1b6b1e19f657"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eefcde1b-d3b8-55ec-9bff-1b6b1e19f657" :answer/id #uuid "eefcde1b-d3b8-55ec-9bff-1b6b1e19f657" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3dca1250-a568-5b14-aa99-ede3c01994fe" :answer-field/id #uuid "3dca1250-a568-5b14-aa99-ede3c01994fe" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-11aba24b-9268-590e-8810-5c57e7e3c410" :answer-field/choices ["answer-11aba24b-9268-590e-8810-5c57e7e3c410"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-11aba24b-9268-590e-8810-5c57e7e3c410" :answer/id #uuid "11aba24b-9268-590e-8810-5c57e7e3c410" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186060935 :tutorial/content "Remember that we can represent a system of two linear equations in two variables using matrices. We can do the same thing for a system of three linear equations in three variables, such as the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+2y\\text{ }-\\text{ }2z=7 \\\\ 2x\\text{ }-\\text{ }1y\\text{ }-\\text{ }4z=2 \\\\ 2x+1y\\text{ }-\\text{ }3z=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor a $3 \\times 3$ system like the one above, we put the coefficients of the system into a $3 \\times 3$ coefficient matrix:\n\n![](images/40/40541d2ecb10c763056ae72734e723a9d5967ed9accaf0bbde6f2a2f9ec96b65.svg)\n\nEach row has the coefficients of one of the equations in the system, and each column consists of the coefficients of one particular variable.\nWe also have the $3 \\times 1$ column vectors\n\n![](images/e5/e56ed72d2d17f9a4bc59bfe51a96534a72ebe481a312b8e9c6c028ade96d3748.svg)\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{b}$ consists of each constant on the right side of the system and $\\mathbf{x}$ contains the variables.\nWith these matrices, we can write our system as $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ or\n\n![](images/f0/f06e5a54e106bcdca8b5cbad677ade3476ba8f6218b4aa79d196f54e0fff3e2c.svg)\n\nWe can write any system of three equations with three variables in this form. Just to check that the above equation is true, let's multiply out the left-hand side to see if it equals the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3x+2y\\text{ }-\\text{ }2z \\\\ 2x\\text{ }-\\text{ }1y\\text{ }-\\text{ }4z \\\\ 2x+1y\\text{ }-\\text{ }3z\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =b\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186059888 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
